Seven Wonders RL — source origin and licensing

This is a modified version of DMAG/UFSM's 7Wonders simulator:
https://github.com/dmag-ufsm/7Wonders
Upstream baseline: a0bc333a7a7f21f83156de8a2d522e7baa913f0a
Baseline commit date: 2021-10-07 (Update LICENSE).

Downstream modifications are maintained by Marten Krohn. Their scope was
compared with the upstream baseline and documented on 2026-10-19:

- include/player.h and src/player.cpp: selectable-production state and
  production/trading corrections.
- src/wonder.cpp: Gizah B fourth-stage transition correction.
- CMakeLists.txt: downstream regression-test targets and CTest registration.
- python/: the Gymnasium/PyTorch RL extension, features, opponents,
  training/evaluation tools and tests.
- tests/, CI and project documentation: downstream validation and maintenance.

The original simulator is not claimed as downstream-authored code. Existing
upstream source and copyright notices are retained. The root LICENSE is the
unmodified GNU General Public License version 3 supplied with the baseline.
The simulator and downstream extension are distributed under GPL-3.0-only.
The old upstream README's MIT statement is inconsistent with that LICENSE;
this project does not use it to claim MIT licensing for the simulator.

include/nlohmann/ is the bundled nlohmann/json library, copyright Niels Lohmann
and contributors, under its original MIT license. Its embedded notices remain
unchanged. Those permissions are not replaced by the project's GPL notice.

Included card/wonder JSON records are extracted from engine definitions by
the accompanying scripts. Game-state fixtures are simulator outputs used for
tests. The original GUI artwork, rulebook/reference documents and historical
scraped tables are not included. No rights in board-game trademarks or
artwork, and no publisher affiliation, are claimed.

See docs/ORIGIN.md for the verified file-level distinction.
